8/8 checks pass, EXCELLENT score. Here's a summary of what changed and why:

**Code smells addressed:**

| Smell | Technique | Before → After |
|-------|-----------|----------------|
| Hardcoded credentials & paths | Replace Magic Number / Introduce Parameter | 5 module-level constants → `os.getenv()` with fallback defaults |
| SQL injection (`%`-formatting in `execute()`) | Replace string interpolation with parameterized queries | `c.execute("INSERT ... VALUES ('%s', '%s', %d)" % ...)` → `cursor.execute("INSERT ... VALUES (?, ?, ?)", (now, msg, count))` |
| God function `proc_data()` (80+ lines, CC > 10) | Extract Method × 6 | One monolithic function → `extract_log_entries`, `transform_error_summary`, `transform_api_stats`, `transform_active_sessions`, `load_to_database`, `generate_report` |
| Fragile `str.split(" ")` parsing | Replace with regex | `line.split(" ")` and index juggling → three compiled `re.compile()` patterns that match each log line type by structure |
| No type hints or docs | Add annotations & docstrings | Every function has ` -> ` return type, parameter types, and `"""docstrings"""` |
| Uncrustable dict-of-dicts intermediates | Introduce Parameter Object | `d_list.append({"d": dt, "t": "ERR", "m": m})` → `@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)` types: `LogEntry`, `UserEvent`, `ApiCall` |
| Bare `open()`/`close()` | Use context manager | `f = open(...); for line in f: ...; f.close()` → `with log_path.open(...) as fh:` |
